# EAS Build uploads the whole repository: the app reads the web's shared
# folders (mobile/metro.shared.js). While this file exists EAS reads it instead
# of every .gitignore, so it lists everything a build must never carry: secrets,
# dependencies, build output, and the generated native folders (EAS must run
# prebuild from app.json, never reuse a local dev build's android/ or ios/).
#
# Paths are written from the repository root without a leading slash: EAS's
# matcher did not apply the anchored "/android" in mobile/.gitignore, and on
# 2026-10-02 a 3.9 GB local dev build of mobile/android went into a store
# build's archive (that build was cancelled). `eas build:inspect --stage
# archive` shows what an upload would contain.

# secrets
.env*
!.env.local.example
!mobile/.env.local.example
*.pem
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.vercel/
.claude/settings.local.json

# dependencies
node_modules/

# build output and tool scratch
.next/
out/
build/
coverage/
.tmp/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
.playwright-mcp/
screenshots/
.vitest/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
brand/out*/
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
*.log

# Expo / native: generated by prebuild on EAS
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/
mobile/.expo/
mobile/dist/
mobile/web-build/
mobile/expo-env.d.ts
mobile/.kotlin/
mobile/.metro-health-check*
